      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Forefoot cushioning is soft and deep from FlyteFoam Turbo+, giving solid impact protection, while the heel feels firmer and more old-school because of the dense lower FlyteFoam and rear rubber.",
        "Responsiveness: The forefoot feels energetic with smooth, rolling toe-offs from the Turbo+ and low-mounted carbon plate, but heel bounce is reduced and can feel dull.",
        "Stability: Stability is the standout trait; a firm lower foam layer, wide midfoot/forefoot platform, low plate setup, secure heel/upper hold, and strong outsole coverage keep landings and transitions very controlled.",
        "Durability: Outsole longevity is a strength, with extensive ASICS Grip coverage (including rear wrap and midfoot areas) that increases wear surface and supports training as well as racing."
